.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt MSR 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm msr
.Nd read and write a processor's model-specific registers
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /dev/cpu/N/msr
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Each processor online has a character device, major 202 and minor
.Ar N ,
its number, through which root reads and writes that processor's
model-specific registers, as Linux's msr driver gives them.
The kernel creates each as root:root with mode 0600 once the processors
are started.
An open needs
.Dv CAP_SYS_RAWIO
in the first user namespace.
.Pp
The file offset is the register's index, cut to 32 bits.
A
.Xr pread 2
or
.Xr read 2
of 8 bytes, or of any multiple of 8, gives the register's 64 bits for
each 8 asked, read again each time, on the device's processor; a
.Xr pwrite 2
or
.Xr write 2
writes the register from each 8 bytes given.
Neither moves the offset.
.Xr lseek 2
takes
.Dv SEEK_SET
and
.Dv SEEK_CUR
alone.
.Pp
The ioctls of
.In asm/msr.h
take an array of eight 32-bit registers, EAX, ECX, EDX, EBX, ESP, EBP,
ESI and EDI, the last four of which some AMD registers read as a key.
.Bl -tag -width X86_IOC_RDMSR_REGS
.It Dv X86_IOC_RDMSR_REGS
Load the registers but ESP from the array, run RDMSR with them, and store
them back.
The descriptor must be open for reading.
.It Dv X86_IOC_WRMSR_REGS
The same with WRMSR.
The descriptor must be open for writing.
.El
.Pp
A write goes through the module parameter
.Pa allow_writes :
.Cm on
lets every write through,
.Cm off
refuses every write, and
.Cm default ,
the value at boot, lets every write through and logs one of them, its
register, program and thread, at most once in 30 seconds.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /sys/devices/virtual/msr/msrN
The device's directory, with dev, uevent and a subsystem link to msr.
.It Pa /sys/class/msr/msrN
.It Pa /sys/dev/char/202:N
Links to that directory, through which udev finds the device.
.It Pa /sys/module/msr/initstate
.Ql live ,
as a loaded
.Pa msr.ko
reads, so that
.Ql modprobe msr
succeeds.
.It Pa /sys/module/msr/parameters/allow_writes
The parameter above, mode 0600.
.El
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EPERM
The caller lacks
.Dv CAP_SYS_RAWIO ,
or a write was made while
.Pa allow_writes
is
.Cm off .
.It Bq Er ENXIO
The processor is not online.
.It Bq Er EIO
The processor has no MSRs, or refused the register with a general
protection fault.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
A transfer's size is not a multiple of 8, or a seek's origin is not
.Dv SEEK_SET
or
.Dv SEEK_CUR .
.It Bq Er EBADF
An ioctl's descriptor is not open for its direction.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
The buffer or array cannot be read or written.
.It Bq Er ENOTTY
The request is unknown.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ioctl 2 ,
.Xr pread 2 ,
.Xr pwrite 2
